WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.102 --> 00:00:19.643
Mabel was supposed to be sleeping at Kathleen's.

2
00:00:20.624 --> 00:00:23.125
And Kathleen was supposed to be sleeping at Mabel's.

3
00:00:24.606 --> 00:00:29.228
Mademoiselle and Mabel's aunt were surprised when the girls woke up in their own homes.

4
00:00:30.668 --> 00:00:34.469
But somehow the girls managed to explain away the adults' questions.

5
00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:39.051
Neither the aunt nor Mademoiselle was angry.

6
00:00:40.451 --> 00:00:44.952
That was good because Kathleen and her brothers wanted to visit the castle that day.

7
00:00:46.973 --> 00:00:49.774
Once again the castle grounds were open to the public.

8
00:00:50.814 --> 00:00:52.855
This time the castle was open too.

9
00:00:54.355 --> 00:00:56.056
There were more visitors than usual.

10
00:00:57.584 --> 00:01:00.546
Everyone in town had heard that Lord Yalding was coming.

11
00:01:00.566 --> 00:01:07.171
"This isn't very much fun," complained Gerald, watching the crowd.

12
00:01:07.191 --> 00:01:11.654
"I hate to see all these people in our garden."

13
00:01:14.096 --> 00:01:17.678
"I said that to the nice caretaker this morning," said Mabel.

14
00:01:17.698 --> 00:01:20.681
"But he didn't seem to mind all the people."

15
00:01:20.701 --> 00:01:24.003
"Did you say anything else?"

16
00:01:24.603 --> 00:01:25.224
asked Jimmy.

17
00:01:26.716 --> 00:01:28.517
"Lots more," said Mabel.

18
00:01:28.537 --> 00:01:30.719
"He's a good listener.

19
00:01:31.259 --> 00:01:33.841
I told him all about our adventures with the ring."

20
00:01:33.861 --> 00:01:36.043
"You didn't!"

21
00:01:36.683 --> 00:01:37.424
said Gerald.

22
00:01:37.444 --> 00:01:39.605
"Don't worry.

23
00:01:39.625 --> 00:01:41.606
He thought I was making everything up.

24
00:01:41.927 --> 00:01:44.088
He told me I should be a writer when I grow up."

25
00:01:45.709 --> 00:01:48.591
"Let's do something with the ring," said Kathleen.

26
00:01:48.611 --> 00:01:52.074
"We can't," said Gerald.

27
00:01:52.094 --> 00:01:55.276
"Mademoiselle said she's coming to meet us."

28
00:01:56.748 --> 00:02:01.591
"But the caretaker said he'd make a picnic for us after everyone left," said Mabel.

29
00:02:01.611 --> 00:02:04.352
"We're supposed to meet him at five o'clock."

30
00:02:04.372 --> 00:02:09.675
"Then you go meet him, and I'll wait for Mademoiselle," said Gerald.

31
00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:12.617
"I don't want you to miss the picnic."

32
00:02:14.178 --> 00:02:18.700
So at five o'clock, Mabel, Kathleen, and Jimmy went to meet the caretaker.

33
00:02:21.802 --> 00:02:24.724
It was a very hot day, and they were grumpy.

34
00:02:26.716 --> 00:02:29.778
They soon saw the caretaker near the edge of some woods.

35
00:02:30.819 --> 00:02:32.820
Two picnic baskets lay on the ground.

36
00:02:37.343 --> 00:02:38.944
making tea," he said.

37
00:02:38.964 --> 00:02:42.787
"There's a little canal just over the ridge.

38
00:02:44.428 --> 00:02:46.529
You can go wading until the tea is ready."

39
00:02:50.732 --> 00:02:52.874
The water was delightfully cool.

40
00:02:54.114 --> 00:02:56.236
Soon the children were in better spirits.

41
00:02:59.532 --> 00:03:01.773
And they were even happier when they had their tea.

42
00:03:02.834 --> 00:03:04.875
Such a feast of cakes and fruit!

43
00:03:06.336 --> 00:03:09.397
"This is like the feast of the gods," said Jimmy.

44
00:03:09.417 --> 00:03:12.379
"What are you talking about?"

45
00:03:12.819 --> 00:03:13.780
asked the caretaker.

46
00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:19.783
Jimmy told him how they had turned into statues and eaten with the gods on the island.

47
00:03:22.004 --> 00:03:24.025
"What big imaginations you all have!"

48
00:03:24.565 --> 00:03:25.586
said the caretaker.

49
00:03:25.606 --> 00:03:30.417
"But everything I told you is true," Jimmy insisted.

50
00:03:30.437 --> 00:03:34.419
"And Mabel told you the truth about the ring too.

51
00:03:35.099 --> 00:03:36.800
Kathleen, give me the ring."

52
00:03:38.301 --> 00:03:40.582
Kathleen reluctantly handed him the ring.

53
00:03:44.525 --> 00:03:47.306
is the ring Mabel told you about," said Jimmy.

54
00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:50.428
"I say it's a wishing ring.

55
00:03:51.148 --> 00:03:54.090
If you wear it and make a wish, your wish will come true."

56
00:03:55.611 --> 00:03:57.332
He gave the ring to the caretaker.

57
00:04:02.328 --> 00:04:05.510
"Don't wish for anything silly," said Kathleen.

58
00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:10.753
"I'll wish for the only thing I really want," said the caretaker.

59
00:04:12.413 --> 00:04:13.554
He closed his eyes.

60
00:04:13.574 --> 00:04:15.855
"I wish that my friend was here."

61
00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:19.857
The three children expected to see a man appear.

62
00:04:22.999 --> 00:04:25.901
But they only saw Gerald and Mademoiselle coming toward them.

63
00:04:32.444 --> 00:04:33.145
said Gerald.

64
00:04:33.165 --> 00:04:41.151
"I persuaded Mademoiselle He stopped talking because Mademoiselle and the caretaker were staring at each other.

65
00:04:41.171 --> 00:04:42.933
"It's you!"

66
00:04:43.453 --> 00:04:44.494
said the caretaker.

67
00:04:44.514 --> 00:04:46.435
"And you!"

68
00:04:46.976 --> 00:04:49.758
said Mademoiselle in an odd, choked voice.

69
00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.001
"Is she your friend?"

70
00:04:53.521 --> 00:04:54.142
asked Jimmy.

71
00:04:54.162 --> 00:04:57.384
"Yes," said the caretaker.

72
00:04:57.404 --> 00:05:00.647
"Jimmy, give your brother some tea.

73
00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:03.108
Mademoiselle, please come walk with me.

74
00:05:03.549 --> 00:05:04.869
I have so much to say to you."

75
00:05:12.432 --> 00:05:17.753
be back in an hour," said Mademoiselle, who suddenly looked younger and more beautiful.

76
00:05:17.773 --> 00:05:23.115
"It has been a long time since Lord Yalding and I have seen each other."
